B.N1=new A.y("confirmDelete",B.a8,"Ask to confirm before a swipe/menu delete removes a row (default off).",B.j,null,!1)
B.eLj=new A.y("builtinDelete",B.a8,"Set false to suppress the engine's own row Delete everywhere it would otherwise appear (long-press row menu AND the default \"delete\" swipe entry) \u2014 default true, exact prior behavior when omitted. Use when the applet declares its OWN guarded delete (e.g. confirms an item count, refuses when shared) so a more-discoverable built-in Delete can't bypass it and orphan data.",B.j,null,!1)
B.eLK=new A.y("bubbles",B.a7,'Opt-in chat-bubble row styling: { byColumn, selfValue, example }. Rows whose byColumn value matches the resolved selfValue (a literal, or a token like $playerId / $rowId / $selected:<table>) render end-aligned + tinted ("me"); everything else (including an unset selfValue token) renders start-aligned + neutral ("them"). Absent entirely -> the plain ListTile row, unchanged. Optional `example: { ids: [...], label, hideLabel, chipLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }` marks demo-content rows (house-design-rules.md rule 10): each listed row id gets a small "example" chip (chipLabel, localizable), a slim label+divider (label, localizable) renders once above the first such row with a Hide action (hideLabel + onHide, an action spec), and when the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\') those rows are dropped from the list entirely. Optional `attachmentsColumn` (chatnest-1029): a column holding inline attachment maps ({name, mime, data}) shown inside the bubble \u2014 image thumbnails and file chips above the text; an attachment-only row shows no empty text line. Absent -> unchanged. Optional markdown (bubbles-markdown-1029): `markdown: true` renders every bubble\'s title text as markdown (bold/italic/lists/code/links; raw HTML shown inert, images never fetched \u2014 alt-text placeholder, links via the checked-link path, code blocks scroll). `markdownColumn: <col>` instead decides PER ROW: markdown only when that column is truthy (true/1/"true"/"1"; falsy/absent = literal text) and takes precedence over `markdown`. `markdownRoles: [..]` limits markdown to rows whose `byColumn` value is in the list (e.g. ["assistant"]). Subtitle/meta stay plain. All absent -> literal text, unchanged. Optional copy (chatx-1031): `selectable: true` makes the bubble text drag-selectable (not installed on touch when copyAction is on, where long-press is the Copy gesture); `copyAction: true` adds a per-message Copy: a hover icon beside the bubble on mouse, and a Copy entry in the long-press / right-click menu. Copies the RAW stored text (markdown source) and toasts "Copied". Both absent -> unchanged. Optional `rowActions` (row-actions-1031): per-message actions, same entry shape and gestures as the list-level `rowActions` prop (takes precedence over it for bubble rows); on mouse they show as a compact icon strip under the hovered/focused bubble. Optional `chat` (chatcap-ui-1031): an AI-chat status layer { statusColumn, noteColumn, thinkingColumn, thinkMsColumn, continuedColumn, sourcesColumn, actionColumn, errorRoles[], labels{thinking,thoughtFor,reasoning,continued,stopped,cutOff,sources,save}, actions{<key>:{label,action}} } (labels are localizable maps; defaults English). Rows in an active status (waiting/thinking/streaming/searching/creating/retrying/continuing) show a spinner / "Thinking\u2026" and render PLAIN text (no markdown reflow); a finished reply shows a collapsible "Thought for {n}s" (PLAIN text, untrusted), the note line, chips (continued / stopped / cut off), a Sources list (http(s) only, via the checked-link path) and, via `actions`, one button keyed by the row\'s actionColumn on an error row (errorRoles, default ["error"]; tinted as an error bubble) or by its status (e.g. truncated). Attachments on non-self rows become file chips with a Save button (host `export` callback, basename-sanitized). Absent -> unchanged. Optional `statusLine: true` (aistatus-1101) replaces the spinner / "Thought for" block with the live status line (animated dots, phase word, elapsed time, running token count), per-tool activity rows (own timer, tap to open the details) from the `steps` column, and, once finished, one quiet summary line ("Thought for 12s \xb7 1.1k tokens") that opens to the steps and the PLAIN-text reasoning. Reads columns startedAt, liveTokens, outputTokens, ms, steps (names overridable with startedAtColumn / liveTokensColumn / outputTokensColumn / msColumn / stepsColumn). `actions.stop` adds a Stop button on the status line; `stepActions{approve,decline}` add Approve / Decline buttons on a waiting step (args: id, step, decision). Words are engine strings (21 languages). Reduced motion keeps the dots still.',B.j,null,!1)
B.eFG=new A.y("selectableThread",B.a8,'Opt-in (chatsel-1031): wraps the bubble list in ONE SelectionArea so a single click-drag selects across many bubbles and Cmd/Ctrl+C copies them in order. Requires `bubbles`; with it on, bubbles use the outer area (per-bubble `selectable` is not double-wrapped), row taps, copyAction buttons and markdown links keep working. Each message carries an invisible role label so copied text reads "You: ..." / "Assistant: ..." (localized; nothing visible changes). Known limit: in a very long lazily built list a drag covers only the rows that are currently built; with selectableThread on, the list builds `threadCacheExtent` px (default 20000, roughly 100 messages) past the viewport, so select-all/drag/copy cover about that much - messages beyond it in a longer thread are not included. Applies to the boxed list (incl. anchor:"bottom") and the windowed root. Mouse platforms (row-actions-1031): bubble text shows the I-beam cursor and primary clicks go to selection (double-click word, triple-click paragraph, shift-click extend; the click focuses the area so Cmd/Ctrl+A selects the thread text and Cmd/Ctrl+C copies); a configured row tap still fires on a plain single click that leaves no selection; a bubble never swipes under a mouse (touch/stylus still do); right-click while text is selected puts "Copy selection" at the top of the row menu. The same mouse rules apply to per-bubble `bubbles.selectable`. Absent -> unchanged.',B.j,null,!1)
B.eSo=new A.y("threadCacheExtent",B.aG,"Opt-in (row-actions-1031), with selectableThread only: how far past the viewport (logical px) the thread is built so selection and copy reach older messages. Default 20000 when selectableThread is on.",B.j,null,!1)
B.f_O=new A.y("rowActions",B.a7,'Opt-in per-row actions (row-actions-1031): a list of entries { id?, icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals?, destructive? } - label is a string or {lang: text} map; action is a normal action spec fired with the ROW (id + table), like cardActions; column + equals/notEquals gates the entry per row (e.g. Edit only where role == "user"). Built-in entries: { builtin: "copy" } copies the row\'s titleColumn text; { builtin: "softDelete", flag?, label?, icon?, beforeAction?, afterAction? } sets the boolean flag column (default "deleted", or the table\'s registered undoSoftDeleteTables flag) to true, hides flagged rows from this list, and shows a "Deleted - Undo" snackbar whose Undo sets it back to false (no confirm dialog). Declaring the entry also registers the table in BoardState.undoSoftDeleteTables so undo/redo never tombstones its rows; declare the flag as a bool column. beforeAction/afterAction are optional action specs fired with the row around the flag write (a nested child whose parent is hidden already shows top-level via parentColumn). Gestures: mouse - hover (or keyboard focus) reveals a \u22ee button on list rows / an icon strip under bubbles, and right-click opens an anchored menu (never a bottom sheet; Esc dismisses; destructive entries last in the error colour). Touch - swipe left reveals the entries as buttons (touch and stylus only, so a mouse drag still selects text and vertical drags still scroll), and long-press opens the same menu at the touch point. Long-press belongs to the menu: like copyAction, per-bubble `selectable` is not installed on touch while rowActions is on (desktop drag-selection and selectableThread are unaffected). Replaces the built-in Open/Edit/Delete row menu and swipeActions for this node; row tap is unchanged. Absent -> unchanged.',B.j,null,!1)
B.f_G=new A.y("parentColumn",B.H,"Opt-in nesting (chatnest-1029): a self-referential column. A row whose parent is another listed row renders indented directly under it (sortColumn/sortDir apply among top-level rows and among siblings); a row whose parent is not listed is top-level. Absent -> the flat list, unchanged.",B.j,null,!1)
B.eGv=new A.y("selectedId",B.T,"Opt-in current-row highlight (chatnest-1029): a row id or a token (e.g. $selected:<table>); the matching row renders as selected (tinted). Unset/unresolved -> no highlight.",B.j,null,!1)
