B.D0=new A.y("emptyTitle",B.T,"Headline for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.j,null,!0)
B.CW=new A.y("emptyText",B.T,"Body text for the empty state; may be a {lang: text} map.",B.j,null,!0)
B.CK=new A.y("emptyAction",B.a7,"Action spec { fn, args } (or bare-string fn) fired by the empty-state button \u2014 e.g. add the first row.",B.j,null,!1)
B.CS=new A.y("emptyActionLabel",B.T,'Label for the empty-state action button (default "Add"); may be a {lang: text} map.',B.j,null,!0)
B.CM=new A.y("emptyActionIcon",B.T,'Icon name for the empty-state action button (default "add").',B.j,null,!1)
B.N2=new A.y("example",B.a7,'Opt-in demo-content marking: { ids, column, label, chipLabel, hideLabel, hiddenFromSetting, onHide }. Exactly one of `ids` (a list of row ids) or `column` (rows where this column is truthy) selects the marked rows \u2014 both or neither makes the block invalid and it is ignored. Marked rows get a small "chipLabel" chip (default "Example"); a slim "label" divider (default "EXAMPLES") renders once above the first marked row with a "hideLabel" (default "Hide") action. `onHide` is an optional action spec { fn, args } fired through normal dispatch; when absent, tapping Hide writes `board.settings[hiddenFromSetting] = true` directly \u2014 no host code required. When the named `hiddenFromSetting` board setting resolves truthy (\'1\'/\'true\'), marked rows are dropped from the node entirely. All labels may be a {lang: text} map.',B.j,null,!1)
