B.eDH=new A.y("choropleth",B.a7,'{ table?, valueColumn, nameColumn?, nameProperty?, color?, lowColor?, highColor?, filter? } \u2014 shade each GeoJSON feature from live rows (min-max normalized). Opt-in `filter`: { "column": <col>, "value": <val-or-token> } (or the set form { "column": <col>, "in": [..] }) scopes the choropleth table\'s rows before shading \u2014 same shape/token resolution as bubl\'s `filter` prop ($selected:<table> \u2192 the selectRow pick, $rowId, $playerId). Absent \u2192 all rows (unchanged); present but resolved to empty (e.g. nothing selected yet) \u2192 no rows shaded. `lowColor`+`highColor` (both required together, any color the theme resolver accepts) swap the default single-hue alpha ramp for a two-hue lerp (e.g. a green\u2192red style ramp); `color` alone keeps the legacy single-hue behavior unchanged.',B.j,null,!1)
