B.f_5=new A.y("sourceLayers",B.a7,'[{ id, sourceLayer, source?, kind: circle|fill|line|heatmap|symbol, minzoom, maxzoom, visible, filter (data-only, validated), label (symbol only, glmap-labels-0810: propertyName | {lang: propertyName} \u2014 same shape as tapLayerDetails\' titleField; resolved against the ambient locale, e.g. {"en":"name","ko":"name_ko"}; default "name" when omitted), paint: { color | colorProp+ramp | colorProp+steps ({numeric-threshold: color} \u2014 the raw-number ramp, V1b; wins over ramp) | colorProp+lowColor+highColor (two-hue continuous ramp, V1a; optional lowValue/highValue domain, default 0..1) | radius | opacity | width | outline | weightProp+weightMax (heatmap weight-from-property; default weightMax 100; add weightInvert: true when LOW values mean high heat) | lowColor+highColor (heatmap: overrides the default density rainbow with a 2-stop low\u2192high ramp) | antialias (fill only, default true: false drops MapLibre\'s per-fill outline pass \u2014 a big raster-cost saving on dense grid surfaces, at the cost of hard polygon edges; use on tiled/gridded fills, not on a few large curvy shapes), textSize/textColor/haloColor/haloWidth/textFont (symbol only; textColor/haloColor accept #hex or {light,dark} \u2014 explicit pinned per-theme colors, never theme-inherited; collision handling is native MapLibre symbol placement \u2014 overlapping labels simply drop, no manual declutter), title: display name for the layerPanel row (string or {lang: text}; default the layer id), filterable: [{ property, label, values: [raw | {value,label}] }] declaring which feature properties the layerPanel may filter this layer by \u2014 options are AUTHORED here because vector-tile features are never enumerated in BoardState, panel: false opts the layer out of the layerPanel, selectedFeature: propertyName | {idProperty} (selfeat-0809: layer draws ONLY the map\'s currently selected feature \u2014 omitted while nothing is selected, filtered to that one feature otherwise; set via a map tap or the mapSelect action; a persistent highlight/halo declares this on its own layer), crossfadeMs: integer (glmap-crossfade-0817, OPT-IN, default 0 = off/instant, byte-identical to pre-crossfade behavior): when > 0, a `mapSetFilter` change on this layer fades over roughly this many ms (twin-layer opacity ramp) instead of snapping \u2014 entering features fade in, leaving features fade out; tap-hit-testing always targets the real layer, never the transient fade twins. Native platforms without a paint-transition-capable backend fall back to an instant swap. } }] \u2014 drawn over the basemap in order. `source` targets an id from tiles (default) or geojsonSources.',B.j,null,!1)
B.eTz=new A.y("tapLayers",B.a7,"List of sourceLayers ids (e.g. a district/dong fill layer) whose features open a detail view on tap, via MapLibre featuresAtPoint. Only checked on a tap that misses every marker; absent/empty = no change. See tapLayerDetails for how a hit resolves to a view.",B.j,null,!1)
B.f_N=new A.y("tapLayerDetails",B.a7,'Optional, keyed by a tapLayers id: { table, idProperty } resolves the tapped feature to a REAL board row (idProperty, default "id", matched against a row id in table) and opens the normal editRow detail; { meterFields: {field: max}, title } instead (or as a fallback when no row resolves) opens a read-only breakdown built from the feature\'s own GeoJSON properties, with a small proportion bar for each meterFields entry. The read-only breakdown also accepts: `fields` (ordered List<String> whitelist of property keys \u2014 only these render, in this order, silently skipping any missing from the feature; absent = every property renders, unchanged); `labels` (Map<String,String>, key -> display name, overriding a row\'s raw-key heading; a key with no entry keeps the raw key); `valueSuffixes` (Map<String,String>, key -> suffix appended after that field\'s rendered value, e.g. " min" \u2014 per-field because mixed rows may need different units); `titleField` (property key used as the sheet title, taking priority over the legacy `title` key; may itself be a {lang: propertyKey} map for a per-locale field preference, e.g. {"en": "name", "ko": "name_ko"}); `valueLabels` ({raw: text|{lang:text}} flat, or {propertyKey: {raw: \u2026}} column-keyed) localizing displayed VALUES with passthrough for unmapped ones; `fieldInfo` ({propertyKey: text|{lang:text}}) adding a small \u24d8 next to that row\'s label that opens a plain-language explainer dialog. labels/valueSuffixes entries also accept {lang: text} maps; `eyebrow` ({lang: text}) is an optional small caption above the title (what KIND of thing this is); `valueColors` (selfeat-0809, {propertyKey: {rawValue: "#hex"}}) renders that row\'s value as a tinted chip instead of plain text \u2014 for a categorical metric the map already colors (a tier/band/class), so the sheet reads the same as the dot that was tapped; `note` ({lang: text}, glmap-tap-honesty-fields 0810) is an optional ONE-LINE plain-language caveat rendered below the field rows, for saying what this sheet does NOT carry (e.g. "Timetables and fares need licensed data \u2014 not included.") instead of leaving the user to wonder why an expected field never appears.',B.j,null,!1)
B.eQL=new A.y("legend",B.a7,'Compact chip-legend strip under the map: { layer: "<sourceLayers id>" } auto-reads that layer\'s paint.ramp, or { entries: {label: color}, title? }. collapsible defaults true (chevron toggle); startCollapsed: true opens with the chips collapsed (title row only \u2014 for narrow layouts; ignored when collapsible is false). Optional valueLabels ({raw: text|{lang:text}}) localizes the displayed entry labels (colors stay keyed by the raw entry; unmapped keys pass through). Absent = no legend, no layout change.',B.j,null,!1)
B.eSl=new A.y("overlay",B.r1,"Opt-in single node (e.g. a chip row) floated OVER the map itself, docked to a corner per overlayAlign \u2014 independent of the below-map legend/nav strip. Stays tappable (normal Stack hit-testing); map gestures still work outside the overlay's own bounds. Absent = no layout change (legacy composition, no Stack wrapper).",B.j,null,!1)
B.csA=s(["topStart","topEnd","bottomStart","bottomEnd"],t.s)
B.eDK=new A.y("overlayAlign",B.bU,"Corner the overlay docks to, 12px inset (default topEnd). Ignored when overlay is unset.",B.csA,null,!1)
B.eOM=new A.y("layerPanel",B.a7,"Opt-in on-map LAYERS control (mapstudio-0814): true, or { align: topStart|topEnd|bottomStart|bottomEnd (default topStart \u2014 the opposite corner from overlayAlign's default, so both may be used together), title, on: false to disable }. Renders a floating card (collapsed = a circular layers button) listing this node's sourceLayers with a visibility toggle each, plus a FILTER popup for any layer declaring `filterable`. It writes the SAME runtime overrides as the mapSetLayerVisible / mapSetFilter actions, so panel state survives rebuilds and agrees with applet-driven buttons. REQUIRES this node's `id` (overrides are keyed by it); an id-less or layer-less glmap renders no panel. A layer declaring selectedFeature is omitted (it draws only the selection); `panel: false` on a layer opts it out. Absent = no panel and NO layout change (no Stack wrapper).",B.j,null,!1)
B.eHo=new A.y("pinMode",B.a8,"Opt-in tap-to-drop multi-pin mode: tapping empty map background (not a marker) appends an ordered pin row {seq, lat, lon} to pinsTable. Existing marker-tap actions are unaffected \u2014 a pin drop only fires when the tap misses every marker. Default off.",B.j,null,!1)
B.eSD=new A.y("pinsTable",B.aW,"Bound table storing dropped pins as ordinary rows (seq/lat/lon) \u2014 persists, exports, clears via normal row ops. Required for pinMode and for the route overlay/legs list below.",B.j,null,!1)
B.eXG=new A.y("routingNodesTable",B.aW,"Table of routable nodes (e.g. transit stations) with lat/lon columns (reuses this node's latColumn/lonColumn). Defaults to `table`.",B.j,null,!1)
B.eSU=new A.y("routingNodeIdColumn",B.H,'Column read as each routing node\'s stable id, matched against routingEdgesAsset feature from/to properties (default "id").',B.j,null,!1)
B.eTK=new A.y("routingNodeNameColumn",B.H,"Column read as a snapped node's display name in a pin's caption (default: this node's labelColumn).",B.j,null,!1)
B.eIS=new A.y("routingNodeAccessoryColumn",B.H,"Optional routingNodesTable column (e.g. a connectivity tier) shown alongside the snapped node name in a pin's caption.",B.j,null,!1)
B.ePN=new A.y("routingEdgesAsset",B.T,"Bundled GeoJSON asset of LineString/MultiLineString edges, each feature carrying routingFromProperty/routingToProperty node-id properties. Builds a headless Dijkstra graph (geo_routing.dart) used to snap pins to nodes and route between consecutive pins.",B.j,null,!1)
